  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &apos;Fires of Dignity: Eco-Cooking and Indigenous Women&#x2019;s Empowerment in Emergency Zones&apos;3, implemented by Solar Inti, aims to empower indigenous women in the emergency zone of Salta (Or&#xe1;n, San Mart&#xed;n, Rivadavia), Argentina, through workshops on building and using ecological cookstoves. Women will learn to cook traditional foods using clean energy and develop micro-enterprises to sell cooked products. The project will directly benefit at least 10 indigenous women from rural communities in the emergency zone. Each woman will represent a family unit of approximately 4 people, reaching a total of 40 direct beneficiaries, with an estimated 30 minors, who will benefit from improved health, nutrition, and living conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
